      "message": "I find this hard to read, and that\u0027s usually not a good idea in security-sensitive code. How about a helper method like:\n\n    private static void isSystemSignaturePermission(Context context, String permission) {\n        try {\n            PermissionInfo permissionInfo \u003d context.getPackageManager().getPermissionInfo(\n                    permission, 0 /* flags */);\n            return \"android\".equals(permissionInfo.packageName);\n        } catch (PackageManager.NameNotFoundException e) {\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\nand then in this code you can just do:\n\n    if (isSystemSignaturePermission(context, REGISTER_NSD_OFFLOAD_ENGINE)) {\n        PermissionUtils.enforceNetworkStackPermissionOr(NETWORK_SETTINGS,\n                REGISTER_NSD_OFFLOAD_ENGINE);\n    } else {\n        PermissionUtils.enforceNetworkStackPermissionOr(NETWORK_SETTINGS);\n    }\n\nIdeally we\u0027d put the helper method in PermissionUtils itself.\n\nIt would also be good to have CTS tests for this method. It should be pretty simple to write:\n\n- On U+, MAINLINE_NETWORK_STACK must never be a system signature permission.\n- NETWORK_SETTINGS must always be a system signature permission.",
